    "meaning": "to let; to leave; to have something done",
    "shortDefinition": "To let, leave, or get something done by someone else."
  },
  "intro": {
    "title": "Let, leave, and get done",
    "paragraphs": [
      "Lassen has three main jobs. Let: Lass mich in Ruhe! (Leave me alone / let me be.) Leave: Ich lasse das Auto zu Hause. And 'have something done': Ich lasse mir die Haare schneiden (I'm having my hair cut).",
      "That last one surprises English speakers. You don't cut your own hair – you let someone do it: lassen + infinitive."
    ]
  },
